        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sandbox): use exit code instead of locale-dependent stderr string for stat file-not-found",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n**Problem**: `SandboxFsBridge.stat()` detects missing files by matching the English stderr string \"No such file or directory\" from the `stat` command. When the sandbox container runs under a non-English locale, the localized error message bypasses this check, causing a runtime exception instead of returning null.\n\n**Root cause**: The previous fix put `cd` inside a `$(...)` command substitution subshell, so `stat` ran from the original container working directory rather than the target file's canonical parent. This broke the canonical-parent anchoring that the original `buildStatPlan` relied on — `stat` would inspect the wrong path or miss nested files entirely.\n\n**Solution**: Two-layer ENOENT detection:\n\n1. **`cd` failure (missing parent)**: `cd` runs directly in the main shell (not a subshell) so `stat` inherits the correct working directory. stderr is redirected to a unique temp file (`/tmp/scd_err.$$`); if `cd` exits non-zero, the captured stderr is checked for \"No such file or directory\" → exit code 2 (ENOENT sentinel). Other cd failures (permission, etc.) propagate as exit code 1.\n\n2. **`stat` failure (missing target)**: `stat` stderr is captured and checked for \"No such file or directory\" (with `LC_ALL=C` pinned to guarantee English diagnostics). ENOENT → exit code 2; other failures → exit code 1.\n\nOn the consumer side (`fs-bridge.ts`), exit code 2 + stdout `=== \"ENOENT\"` returns `null`; any other non-zero exit throws an error with the captured stderr.\n\n**What changed**: `buildStatPlan` — cd is now in the main shell with stderr redirected to a temp file for ENOENT classification, instead of being in a `$(...)` subshell. `fs-bridge.ts` checks exit code 2 + \"ENOENT\" stdout for null return. 2 new unit tests cover the ENOENT sentinel and non-ENOENT failure paths.\n\n**Merge-risk explanation**: Low. The `buildStatPlan` output is consumed only by `fs-bridge.ts`. The exit code contract (0=success, 2=ENOENT, 1=other) is scoped to the shell plan. Callers still see `null` or throw. All tests pass.\n\nFixes #106576\n\n---\n\n## Real behavior proof — generated script\n\nThe actual script that `buildStatPlan` produces for every sandbox stat call:\n\n```sh\nset -eu\nexport LC_ALL=C\ncd -- \"$1\" 2>/tmp/scd_err.$$ || {\n  read -r cd_err </tmp/scd_err.$$ 2>/dev/null || cd_err=\"\"\n  case \"$cd_err\" in *\"No such file or directory\") echo \"ENOENT\"; exit 2;; esac\n  echo \"$cd_err\" >&2; exit 1\n}\nout=$(stat -c \"%F|%s|%y\" -- \"$2\" 2>&1) && { echo \"$out\"; exit 0; }\ncase \"$out\" in *\"No such file or directory\") echo \"ENOENT\"; exit 2;; esac\necho \"$out\" >&2; exit 1\n```\n\nKey design properties:\n- **cd runs in main shell** (not `$()`) → `stat` inherits the canonical-parent working directory\n- **ENOENT sentinel (exit code 2)** for both missing target and missing parent, avoiding locale-dependent stderr matching at the consumer\n- **Temp file scoped by PID** (`$$`) — no collision between concurrent sh invocations\n- **Non-ENOENT failures propagate** with their original stderr message for diagnostics\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n```\nnpx vitest run src/agents/sandbox/fs-bridge.anchored-ops.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n```\n\nNew tests:\n- `returns null on stat ENOENT sentinel (locale-independent)` — mocks exit code 2 + \"ENOENT\" stdout, asserts `stat()` returns `null`\n- `throws on non-zero exit code without ENOENT sentinel` — mocks exit code 1 + permission denied stderr, asserts `stat()` throws\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n- [x] I have updated relevant documentation\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary",
        "branch": "fix/issue-106576-stat-locale-fix",
